@startuml
!include _style.puml
title Order State: Seller Sub-Order Lifecycle
hide empty description
[*] --> PENDING_PAYMENT : OrderDraftFactory.create()
PENDING_PAYMENT --> WAITING_SELLER_CONFIRM : successful payment
WAITING_SELLER_CONFIRM --> PREPARING : sellerAcceptOrder()\n[owning active seller; group PAID/PARTIALLY_REFUNDED]
PREPARING --> SHIPPED : assignTrackingNumber()\n[owning seller; paid group; valid courier/tracking]
SHIPPED --> COMPLETED : confirmOrderDelivered() [customer owner]\nor autoConfirmDelivered() [scheduler eligible]
COMPLETED --> COMPLETED : confirmOrderDelivered()\n[customer owner] / no-op
PENDING_PAYMENT --> CANCELLED : customerCancelOrder()\n[owner; nonblank reason]\nor orchestration payment failure
WAITING_SELLER_CONFIRM --> CANCELLED : sellerRejectOrder() [paid; reason]\nor customerCancelOrder() [owner; reason]
PREPARING --> CANCELLED : customerCancelOrder()\n[owner; nonblank reason]
SHIPPED --> CANCELLED : Admin partial/full refund\n[refundable payment]
COMPLETED --> CANCELLED : Admin partial refund\n[refundable payment]
CANCELLED --> CANCELLED : customerCancelOrder()\n[owner; nonblank reason] / no-op

note right of CANCELLED
Customer cancellation accepts PENDING_PAYMENT,
WAITING_SELLER_CONFIRM and PREPARING.
Seller rejection/customer cancellation restore stock;
paid orders also invoke partial refund for the shop total.
Orchestration failure releases all reserved stock.
Admin refund methods can cancel orders without restoring stock:
partial refund has no source-order-status guard;
full refund cancels every non-COMPLETED sub-order.
end note
note left of WAITING_SELLER_CONFIRM
PaymentService callback updates null, PENDING_PAYMENT
or existing WAITING_SELLER_CONFIRM orders only.
It does not resurrect CANCELLED/COMPLETED orders.
Its failure path leaves order states and stock unchanged.
end note
note right of COMPLETED
Receipt sets completedAt, without changing Shipment.
Auto-confirm runs hourly for SHIPPED orders
whose shippedAt is before now minus 7 days.
The 24h unconfirmed-order scheduler queries shippedAt,
not createdAt; ordinary waiting orders have no shippedAt.
end note
